_In general, to oversee all policies and actions that have been or will be carried out by the Board of Directors, the Board of Commissioners performs its supervisory function through joint meetings with the Board of Directors and/or the General Meeting of Shareholders (GMS), as well as through working visits or monitoring activities. The Board of Commissioners routinely conducts oversight of the performance of the Board of Directors and the Company on a monthly basis, and whenever matters require a response or input, the Board of Commissioners provides such feedback either in writing—through formal correspondence—or orally during meetings with the Board of Directors. The meetings are held to obtain comprehensive explanations from the Board of Directors regarding the Company’s current issues, and to enable the Board of Commissioners to provide advice and direction on matters faced by the Company. The results of such meetings are documented in minutes of meetings, and issues requiring follow-up are conveyed to the Board of Directors in the form of a letter containing the advice or recommendations of the Board of Commissioners, to be acted upon by the Board of Directors and/or used as material for the GMS. Furthermore, the results of the Board of Commissioners’ supervision of the management and operations of the Company conducted by the Board of Directors are reported to the Shareholders/GMS on a quarterly and annual basis, with details as follows:_

